  "moments": [
    {
      "id": "diez-a-diez",
      "title": {
        "es": "Veinte partidas y todo igual",
        "en": "Twenty games, still level"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "Con la victoria de Steinitz en la partida 20, el marcador quedó 10 a 10, con ocho triunfos por bando. El match siguió hasta que alguien sumara diez victorias.",
        "en": "Steinitz's win in game 20 left the score 10–10, with eight wins each. The match went on until someone reached ten wins."
      },
      "round": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "peon-perdido",
      "title": {
        "es": "Un peón regalado",
        "en": "A pawn thrown away"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "En la partida 22, Chigorin jugó 9...Cxd5?, un error elemental que perdía un peón; después su alfil quedó atrapado y Steinitz ganó.",
        "en": "In game 22, Chigorin played 9...Nxd5?, an elementary error that lost a pawn; his bishop was later trapped and Steinitz won."
      },
      "round": 22,
      "ply": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "mate-en-dos",
      "title": {
        "es": "El mate en dos que decidió el título",
        "en": "The mate in two that decided the title"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "En la partida 23, Chigorin tenía una pieza de más y la partida ganada, pero jugó 32.Ab4?? y Steinitz respondió 32...Txh2+, con mate inevitable. Chigorin abandonó y Steinitz retuvo el título.",
        "en": "In game 23, Chigorin was a piece up and winning, but played 32.Bb4?? and Steinitz replied 32...Rxh2+, with unstoppable mate. Chigorin resigned and Steinitz kept the title."
      },
      "round": 23,
      "ply": 63
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Entre 1890 y 1891 jugaron por telégrafo dos partidas que empezaban con el gambito Evans, con tres días por jugada. Chigorin ganó las dos, y ese interés del público llevó a la revancha.",
        "en": "In 1890–91 they played two games by telegraph cable, both starting from the Evans Gambit, with three days per move. Chigorin won both, and the public interest led to the rematch."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1892"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "La Sociedad de Ajedrez de San Petersburgo y el Club de Ajedrez de La Habana ofrecieron organizar el match; Steinitz eligió La Habana.",
        "en": "Both the St. Petersburg Chess Society and the Havana Chess Club offered to host; Steinitz chose Havana."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1892"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Si llegaban a nueve victorias cada uno, el match terminaba empatado y Steinitz conservaba el título.",
        "en": "Had both players reached nine wins, the match would have ended drawn and Steinitz would have kept the title."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1892"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Las partidas se jugaron en el Centro Asturiano de La Habana.",
        "en": "The games were played at the Centro Asturiano in Havana."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "OlimpBase",
        "url": "https://www.olimpbase.org/ind-wcc/wc1892-wch.html"
      }
    }
